<title>GERMANY: Ford reaches pact with German workers over Fiesta.</title>
<headline>Ford reaches pact with German workers over Fiesta.</headline>
<dateline>COLOGNE, Germany 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German unit of U.S. carmaker Ford Motor Co has agreed to a cost-savings programme with its works council to keep production of the Ford Fiesta in Germany, a newspaper said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Cologne Stadt-Anzeiger said in its Thursday edition that the pact between Ford and the council, which represents company workers, would save about 27 million marks ($17.6 million) annually.</p>
<p>Ford is expected to announce details of the pact on Friday that will affect about 1,500 workers.</p>
<p>A company spokesman could not be reached for comment since the company was closed on Thursday for a national holiday.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.533 German Marks)</p>
</text>
